IDBL - Identifier name should begin in lowercase letter (CG#6) unless acronym
FNBL - Function name should begin in lowercase letter (CG#7) unless acronym
CNBU - Class name should begin in uppercase letter (CG#4)
FDOC - Function should be defined outside of class (CG#15)
NOE - Type allocates memory on heap, needs operator  =  (CG#34)
NCC - Type allocates memory on heap, needs copy constructor (CG#34)
OERETC -  Operator = should should return type const & (CG#35)
OECAS - Operator = should check for assignment to self (CG#35)
NAOE - Not assigned in operator = (CG#35)
OECOE - Operator = should call other operator = (CG#35)
OERT- Operator = should return "*this".  (CG#37)
ILNA - Members should be initialized in initializer lists, not assignments. (CG#38)
ILOD - Initializer lists should initialize members in the order declared. (CG#39)
InV - Do not use in-line constructors, destructors or virtual functions.  CG#47
InCD - Do not use in-line constructors, destructors or virtual functions. CG#47
NMF - Do not use mallocs or frees. Use new/delete CG#50
ONND - Operator New but no delete  CG #52
ODNN - Vice versa CG #52
BCVD - Base class should have virtual destrucotr CG #55
RDPF - Redefines default parameter for function CG# 56
RINVF - Redefines inherited, non virtual function CG# 57
OMBM - Operator %s must be a member Current coding guideline number #68
OSBM - Operator %s should be a member Current coding guideline number #69
OSNBM - Operator %s should NOT be a member Current coding guideline number #70
